<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Middle Fork Big Sheep Creek and Bonny Lakes to Dollar Lake Pass</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:357-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.208937" lon="-117.071582"><ele>1856.7</ele><name>Salt Creek Summit Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:salt-creek-summit-sno-park (= OSM parking 'Salt Creek Summit Sno-Park', way 306035418); not moved; confidence: high; pdf_page: 357; book_elev_ft: 6150; quote: Salt Creek Summit (6,150 feet) is on Road 39; map 97: SALT CREEK SUMMIT SNO-PARK 6150'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.174440" lon="-117.089820"><ele>1952.7</ele><name>Wagon Road Trail top, above the Big Sheep shelter</name><desc>source: high point (DEM 6,406 ft) of OSM Tenderfoot Wagon Road TR 1819 (way 1099205317), 3.53 mi from the sno-park, where the trail starts its descent to the hut (OSM path end 45.1721,-117.0926; CalTopo 1DSM9 'Big Sheep Hut' 45.1717,-117.0913); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 359; quote: The last 0.5 mile descends steeply to the shelter on the Cutoff Trail ... do not descend the 0.5-mile trail to the shelter, but continue west</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.177520" lon="-117.103400"><ele>1972.6</ele><name>Tenderfoot Wagon Road summer trail, east end</name><desc>source: east end of OSM Tenderfoot Wagon Road TR 1819 way 661645954 (meets Forest Road 100); DEM 6,472 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 360; quote: follow the trail to the wilderness boundary ... Continue on the north side of the creek all the way, often out of sight, and follow the summer trail as best you can</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.184910" lon="-117.161100"><ele>2373.0</ele><name>Bonny Lakes</name><desc>source: point on OSM Bonny Lakes Trail TR 1803 in the flat at 7,770-7,830 ft (DEM 7,785) 3.84 mi along 1819/1803 from wp 3; no named lake in OSM; confidence: low; pdf_page: 360; book_elev_ft: 7800; quote: Ski above (north of) this, and in several hundred yards reach Bonny Lakes at 7,800 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.193070" lon="-117.182610"><ele>2546.7</ele><name>Dollar Lake Pass</name><desc>source: high point of OSM Bonny Lakes Trail TR 1803 (DEM 8,355 ft) between Bonny Lakes and Dollar Lake (OSM way 537282532, 400 m SW); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 361; book_elev_ft: 8400; quote: Climb to Dollar Lake Pass at 8,400 feet. The wide, flat saddle gives fine views</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Middle Fork Big Sheep Creek and Bonny Lakes to Dollar Lake Pass</name><desc>1. Salt Creek Summit Sno-Park -&gt; Wagon Road Trail top, above the Big Sheep shelter: osm (high), 3.63 mi | 2. Wagon Road Trail top, above the Big Sheep shelter -&gt; Tenderfoot Wagon Road summer trail, east end: straight (low), 0.69 mi | 3. Tenderfoot Wagon Road summer trail, east end -&gt; Bonny Lakes: osm (medium), 3.84 mi | 4. Bonny Lakes -&gt; Dollar Lake Pass: osm (medium), 1.40 mi</desc>
